       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for ibuprofen in adults is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. Over-the-counter use is limited to 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg in one dose is double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.\n- **Risks at this dose:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't make it safe.\n\nTypical oral adult regimens are:\n- **Mild to moderate pain:** 400 mg every 4\u20136 hours as needed.\n- **Inflammatory or arthritic conditions:** 400\u2013800 mg three to four times daily. This is at most 3,200 mg/day, and the lowest effective dose is preferred.\n\n**Possible typo:** Did you mean 400 mg or 800 mg rather than 1600 mg? Or did you mean 1600 mg total per day, split into smaller doses?\n\nPlease confirm the dose, frequency, and indication, and I'll enter it right away. For example, I could enter ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day) or 400 mg PO four times daily. It's also worth reviewing the order with your resident or attending before it's placed."
      }
